sequenceDiagram
  accTitle: Custom video room architecture
  accDescr: A browser uses separate producer and consumer PeerConnections. A Worker authenticates HTTP requests and calls a room Durable Object, which owns application state and uses server credentials to manage two Realtime SFU sessions. A hibernating WebSocket sends revision-only notifications.

  participant Browser as Browser participant
  box rgb(251, 227, 207) Trusted application boundary
    participant Worker as Worker
    participant Room as Room Durable Object
  end
  box rgb(224, 235, 255) Realtime SFU
    participant Publish as Producer session
    participant Subscribe as Consumer session
  end

  Note over Browser,Room: Access identity + member capability<br/>HTTP owns snapshots, SDP, and mutations
  Browser->>Worker: Authenticated HTTP request
  Worker->>Room: Typed RPC
  Room-->>Worker: Tagged result
  Worker-->>Browser: Authorized JSON + SDP

  Note over Browser,Subscribe: Separate producer and consumer PeerConnections<br/>Separate per-session SDP queues
  Room->>Publish: SFU API with server credential
  Browser->>Publish: Publish audio + video
  Room->>Subscribe: SFU API with server credential
  Subscribe-->>Browser: Remote audio + video

  Browser->>Worker: WebSocket upgrade + single-use ticket
  Worker->>Room: fetch() for upgrade only
  Room-->>Browser: room-changed revision
  Note over Browser,Room: Notification triggers an authorized HTTP snapshot
